From 2e2213cc13693fafaabfc914225af28fe3b553e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:00:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fold corrected 735-village control-group DiD results into
 paper, dashboard, and citation; add Dev Log Entry 15

The village-list/checkpoint resume-logic fix from the previous commit
worked, but its first invocation silently did nothing: village_id is a
sequential index reassigned on every regeneration, so the old 753-row
checkpoint (all filled in) matched every one of the new 735-village
list's rows by index and the extraction skipped straight to done
without a single new Earth Engine call. Caught this before trusting
the resulting numbers, by independently reproducing did_model.py's
output against the still-committed old 753-row data and finding it
matched byte-for-byte -- then diagnosed, fixed, and verified the
resume-logic bug itself (coordinate-match instead of village_id-match,
tested against both the same-list and regenerated-list cases).

After the corrected rerun was pushed, independently verified rather
than trusted: confirmed 735 rows / 0 duplicate coordinates in the
village list, confirmed the two control-results CSVs have per-row
image-count columns that vary (evidence of genuine EE calls, not a
skipped extraction), and reran did_model.py locally against the
pulled data -- reproducing the previously-pasted terminal numbers
to the 5th decimal place.

Two real findings, not just tighter precision:
- Summer NDBI DiD holds and tightens: +0.0322, p=0.00033 (was
  +0.0377, p=0.0021). Full-year NDBI DiD stays non-significant:
  +0.0088, p=0.275 (was +0.0082, p=0.215).
- Night-lights DiD flips from a reported null in both windows to a
  significant positive gap in both: summer +0.1413, p=0.0044 (both
  specs agree); full-year +0.1653, p=0.036 under fixed effects but
  p=0.103 without them (spec-dependent, flagged as such). This is
  NOT an absolute rise in treated villages -- Section 4.3's
  treated-only Wilcoxon test on the same summer window is still a
  clean null (p=0.9999) -- it's control villages' night-lights
  falling over the same period while treated villages held flat.

Baseline-imbalance disclosure expanded from NDBI-only to all four
outcome/window combinations: 3 of 4 are now significantly imbalanced
at baseline (all but NDBI full-year), with night-lights full-year
the most imbalanced and also the one combination where the two DiD
specifications disagree -- a plausible link, flagged as such rather
than asserted.

Updated: BO_Research_Paper.md (Abstract, S3.1, S4.6 rewritten with
an explicit bug/correction note, S6.7, Discussion, Conclusion, S7.5),
README.md, BO_Executive_Summary.md (checklist gains a Night-Lights
DiD row), CITATION.cff (735-village count, v1.1.1), DATA_DICTIONARY.md,
app.py, dashboard pages 1/5/7/8 (5_Statistical_Validation.py gains a
Night-Lights DiD card pair, no longer a null not worth displaying),
did_model.py's docstring, make_control_multiyear_maps.py's map title.
Regenerated Figure 8 (reads live from the DiD summary JSONs, so no
hardcoded numbers to fix there), its interactive counterpart, all
three doc PDFs via build_docs_pdfs.sh, and BORDER_OPTICS_Maps_and_Plots.pdf.
Added Development Log Entry 15 documenting the full sequence.

